---
// Privacy policy. Describes what the site actually collects and who it goes to; keep it in step with the code.
// The owner's own answers (how long records are kept, who to contact) live in `privacy` in src/data/site.js.
// This is a plain-language draft based on PIPEDA, not legal advice.
import Notice from '../components/Notice.astro'
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { location, phone, privacy, site } from '../data/site.js'

const missing = !privacy.keepRecordsFor || !privacy.contactName || !privacy.contactEmail
const updated = new Date(`${privacy.lastUpdated}T12:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString('en-CA', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' })
const tbc = 'rounded bg-cream px-1.5 font-semibold text-maroon'
const h2 = 'section-title mt-10 mb-3 text-[26px]'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Firearms Academy Canada collects, uses and protects your personal information."
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">What we collect when you register or contact us, why, who sees it, and your choices.</Fragment>

  <article class="body-text max-w-[760px]">
    {
      missing && (
        <Notice title="Draft">
          This policy is not final. Parts marked “to be confirmed” are waiting for answers from {site.name}.
        </Notice>
      )
    }

    <p class="mt-6">
      {site.name} (“we”) teaches the Canadian Firearms Safety Course (CFSC) and the Canadian Restricted Firearms Safety Course (CRFSC) at{' '}
      {location.name}, {location.address}. We are responsible for the personal information we collect, and we handle it according to
      Canada’s Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA). Last updated {updated}.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What we collect</h2>
    <ul class="grid list-disc gap-2 pl-5">
      <li>
        <b>When you register:</b> your name and nickname, phone numbers, email address, the course and weekend you choose, whether you already
        have the student guide, a friend you would like to sit with, any comments, and whether you want to move to an earlier class if a space
        opens. For restricted-only courses, we also ask when you completed the non-restricted (PAL) course and who taught it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>About your payment:</b> the amount, how you paid, the date, and your payment reference. We never see your bank or card details:
        Interac e-Transfers are sent through your own bank.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>On course day:</b> whether a signed under-18 consent form was received, whether you attended, and short notes from your instructor.
        The consent form itself stays on paper with us.
      </li>
      <li><b>When you contact us:</b> your name, email address and message.</li>
      <li>
        <b>When you visit the website:</b> like any website, our hosting provider handles your IP address and browser details to deliver the
        pages and protect the site from abuse. Public pages set no cookies and use no analytics or advertising trackers. Only staff who sign in
        to our booking system get a sign-in cookie.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">We do not ask for your date of birth, your licence (PAL) number, or copies of ID.</p>

    <h2 class={h2}>How we use it</h2>
    <ul class="grid list-disc gap-2 pl-5">
      <li>To book your seat, match your payment to your registration, and confirm your place.</li>
      <li>
        To email you about your booking: the payment details after you register, your course confirmation, a reminder before the course,
        and any change or cancellation.
      </li>
      <li>To prepare the class list and run the course.</li>
      <li>To answer your questions.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We do not sell your information, and we do not send newsletters or promotional emails. If that ever changes, we will ask you first.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Who sees it</h2>
    <ul class="grid list-disc gap-2 pl-5">
      <li><b>Our owner</b> sees all registrations and payments.</li>
      <li>
        <b>Your instructors</b> see the class list for the weekends they teach: your name, contact details, course, payment status (paid or
        not, without amounts) and course-day notes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Service providers</b> that run the website for us and may only use your information for that purpose:{' '}
        <a class="link" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cloudflare</a> (website hosting),{' '}
        <a class="link" href="https://www.mongodb.com/legal/privacy/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MongoDB Atlas</a>{' '}
        (where registrations are stored), and{' '}
        <a class="link" href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Resend</a> (sends our emails).
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Google</b> provides the website’s fonts and the map on our <a class="link" href="/locations">location page</a>; loading them
        sends your IP address to Google.
      </li>
      <li>Anyone the law requires us to share it with.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      These providers may store or process information outside Canada, including in the United States, where it may be accessible to
      authorities under the laws of that country.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep registration records for {privacy.keepRecordsFor || <span class={tbc}>to be confirmed</span>} after your course, then delete
      them. Contact-form messages are kept for the same period. Email records kept by our email provider are deleted on its own schedule.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>How we protect it</h2>
    <p>
      Only our staff can open the booking system, each with their own password, and instructors see only their own classes. Every change to a
      registration is recorded with who made it. Information travels over encrypted (HTTPS) connections, and our database provider encrypts
      the stored data. If a breach ever creates a real risk of significant harm, we will tell you and the Privacy Commissioner of Canada, as
      the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Students under 18</h2>
    <p>
      Students under 18 may take the course with a signed parent or guardian <a class="link" href="/consent">consent form</a>. We record only
      that the form was received.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to see the information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or withdraw your consent. If you withdraw consent before
      your course, we may not be able to keep your registration. We will answer within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or requests, contact {privacy.contactName || <span class={tbc}>name to be confirmed</span>} at{' '}
      {privacy.contactEmail ? <a class="link" href={`mailto:${privacy.contactEmail}`}>{privacy.contactEmail}</a> : <span class={tbc}>email to be confirmed</span>},
      or call <a class="link" href={phone.href}>{phone.display}</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you are not satisfied with our answer, you can complain to the{' '}
      <a class="link" href="https://www.priv.gc.ca/en/report-a-concern/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
